      "side": 1,
      "message": "Technically, that depends on the numerator, right? The largest finite half-float is 65504, so until your numerator is ~4, you should be able to do the divide. I do plan to use this value in the denominator guard for the luminosity fix (my recent tryjobs confirmed that a large enough value fixes the intel mac issues). But the exact nature of the failure is still hard to reason about fully.\n\nMost likely, the value we\u0027re dividing by is much smaller than this in some cases. We really want to know the relative magnitude of the two values, but that\u0027s not practical. Ideally we\u0027d be able to handle this like we do on CPU:\n\n```\nfloat result \u003d x / y;\nif (!isfinite(result)) { ... }\n```\n\n... but of course, we can\u0027t rely on infinity/nan, so we\u0027re stuck with this crude approximation. Oh well.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 150,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 150,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "acbeb497fa81eb29a187ec2cf3967390fa523c8f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
