      "writtenOn": "2024-08-16T18:14:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I added some more comments to explain that even just that check isn\u0027t safe.\n\nI believe that for just the division itself, you need `d \u003e\u003d x/65504`, so for this particular value you\u0027re safe up to ~4 as you figured. But for values \u003c 4, since it\u0027s the fixed guard of $kMinNormalHalf and not `x/65504`, you\u0027ll have more low numerators that could have been divided by a smaller denominator hit the \"denominator\u003d0 fallback\" code. So the values that go through the non-fallback code end up being not as close to the f16 max, which probably avoids any further opportunities to overflow with subsequent operations.",
      "parentUuid": "1a622b08_2226d273",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 150,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 150,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "acbeb497fa81eb29a187ec2cf3967390fa523c8f",
